  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(MOE) Strengthening climate resilience through flood and drought management in Central Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Active</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to strengthen the climate and disaster resilience of people and communities in vulnerable regions of the Kyrgyz Republic and Uzbekistan through integrated and effective water resources management techniques. The project cost is US$ 10million for 4 years (2023-2026) funded by the Ministry of Environment, ROK.</narrative>
